      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The enforcement regime produced a measurable outcome: year-to-date crossings near multi-decade lows under asylum shutdown and deportation policies. Yet the system registered a shift in the flow—apprehensions from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March along the southwest border, spurred by milder spring weather. The policy architecture held firm even as the seasonal catalyst applied new pressure. Lawmakers, the architects of the deadlock, remained stalled over separate funding for immigration enforcement agencies in a pending reconciliation package.",
