    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The data revealed a change in the pattern: apprehensions increased from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March along the southwest border. The seasonal catalyst—milder spring weather—drove the statistical trend, yet the deep structure held firm with year-to-date crossings near multi-decade lows. Observers of the machinery noted the enforcement apparatus maintained its border security effect even as the system's components failed to align on funding. Political deadlock persisted over immigration enforcement agencies.",
